 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? Totally normal. People worry about it all the time. What's the worst that happens? You leave before our food gets to you. Go with group that knows each other, and try to stick together. If someone falls behind, the waiter usually helps. Come as you are. If you worry about few extra pounds or fashion mistakes, think of how much money you' spending anyway. Most people don't. Ask for descriptions, it helps. And if you' still unsure, order a sample of something simple like pasta. Definitely. You get to try a bit of everything, and it' a great way to spot things you might like.",
